fs/dax: look up an entry's folio only when it has one

dax_disassociate_entry() and dax_busy_page() compute dax_to_folio(entry)
before they return early for zero and empty entries. dax_to_folio() is
page_folio(pfn_to_page(dax_to_pfn(entry))), and page_folio() reads the
page's compound_head. An empty entry's pfn is 0, so the lookup reads the
struct page of physical page 0.

Where page 0 has no struct page, that read faults. An arm64 guest whose RAM
starts at 0x80000000 oopses on its first DAX fault that replaces an empty
entry, as when it execs a binary from an EROFS image mounted with
dax=always over virtio-pmem (shards guests):

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address fffffdffbe000008
  pc : dax_disassociate_entry.isra.0+0x20/0x50
  lr : dax_insert_entry+0xc0/0x230
  Call trace: dax_disassociate_entry <- dax_fault_iter <- dax_iomap_pte_fault
    <- dax_iomap_fault <- erofs_dax_fault <- __do_fault <- do_read_fault

Check the entry first, as both functions mean to. Mainline has the same
code at v7.2-rc4.

--- a/fs/dax.c
+++ b/fs/dax.c
@@ -468,21 +468,20 @@
 static void dax_disassociate_entry(void *entry, struct address_space *mapping,
 				bool trunc)
 {
-	struct folio *folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
-
 	if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
 		return;
 
-	dax_folio_put(folio);
+	dax_folio_put(dax_to_folio(entry));
 }
 
 static struct page *dax_busy_page(void *entry)
 {
-	struct folio *folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
+	struct folio *folio;
 
 	if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
 		return NULL;
 
+	folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
 	if (folio_ref_count(folio) - folio_mapcount(folio))
 		return &folio->page;
 	else
